{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>By standards.</b> Each standard had a sign — a coloured cloth hanging on it; the colour of this one not like the colour of that one. The colour of each corresponds to its stone set in the breastplate, and from this each one would recognize his standard. Another interpretation: בְּאֹתֹת לְבֵית אֲבֹתֵיהֶם — by the sign that Jacob their father handed down to them when they carried him up from Egypt, as stated (Genesis 50): ״וַיַּעֲשׂוּ בָנָיו לוֹ כֵן כַּאֲשֶׁר צִוָּם״ — Judah, Issachar, and Zebulun carried him from the east; Reuben, Simeon, and Gad from the south, etc. — as found in Tanḥuma in this perasha." "<b>Far off.</b> At a distance of a mil, as stated in Joshua: ״אַךְ רָחוֹק יִהְיֶה בֵּינֵיכֶם וּבֵנָיו כְּאַלְפַּיִם אַמָּה״ (Joshua 3) — so that they could come on Shabbat. Moses and Aaron and his sons and the Levites camp adjacent to it."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:09:13.682662552Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}